450: ## 4. Zero-Allocation Streaming Architecture
451: 
452: ### 4.1 In-Place Decryption Topology
453: High-throughput telemetry processing requires parsing gigabyte-scale flight logs with zero GC pressure and zero heap allocations.
454: 
455: ```text
456: Log Buffer: [ ... | Type | Len | Seed | Encrypted Ciphertext ... | 0xFF | ... ]
457:                      │      │     │                 │
458:                      │      │     └─────────┬───────┘
459:                      ▼      ▼               ▼
460:       RawRecordEnvelope<'a>             [XOR Keystream]
461:                │                                │
462:                │   out_buf: [ ... scratch buffer (e.g. 1024 B on stack) ... ]
463:                │                 │
464:                │                 ▼
465:                │      Step 1: Write XOR-descrambled Ciphertext into out_buf
466:                │                 │
467:                │                 ▼
468:                │      Step 2: Read next_iv = out_buf[len - 16 .. len]
469:                │                 │
470:                │                 ▼
471:                │      Step 3: AES-256-CBC Decrypt in-place inside out_buf
472:                │                 │
473:                │                 ▼
474:                │      Step 4: PKCS7 Unpad in-place (adjust slice boundary)
475:                │                 │
476:                │                 ▼
477:                │      Step 5: ivs[fp] = next_iv
478:                │                 │
479:                ▼                 ▼
480:         Telemetry Record Parser (e.g. OsdRecord::parse(plaintext_slice))
481: ```
482: 
483: ### 4.2 Stack-Allocated Caller Example
484: ```rust
485: let header = TxtHeader::parse(&file_bytes)?;
486: let mut iter = RecordEnvelopeIterator::new(&file_bytes, &header)?
487:     .with_key(1, base_key, base_iv)
488:     .with_key(10, gimbal_key, gimbal_iv);
489: 
490: // Fixed 1KB scratch buffer reused across millions of iterations
491: let mut scratch = [0u8; 1024];
492: 
493: while let Some(env_res) = iter.next() {
494:     let env = env_res?;
495:     let plaintext = iter.decode_into(&env, &mut scratch)?;
496:     
497:     match env.record_type {
498:         1 => {
499:             let osd = OsdRecord::parse(plaintext)?;
500:             // Process telemetry with ZERO allocations
501:         }
502:         3 => {
503:             let gimbal = GimbalRecord::parse(plaintext)?;
504:         }
505:         _ => {}
506:     }
507: }
508: ```
